# Measured metals (exact conductor Fresnel from a complex IOR): an aluminium
# mirror, then copper at roughness 0.15, titanium at 0.35, gold at 0.6 and
# aluminium at 0.9, and a silver one in front, under a rectangular light and
# a dim uniform sky. Against the same model in Mitsuba ("mypbr" BSDFs) it
# should match; against Mitsuba's own conductor / roughconductor ("native":
# its own spectral data reduced to RGB, separable Smith G, no energy
# compensation) the mirror and the smooth spheres should match and the rough
# ones come out brighter in mypbr.

image_width  384
aspect_ratio 2
samples_per_pixel 512
max_depth    64
background   0.15 0.15 0.15

camera lookfrom 0 2.2 9  lookat 0 0.6 0  vup 0 1 0  vfov 24

material floor  lambertian 0.5 0.5 0.5
material wall   lambertian 0.3 0.35 0.4
material lamp   emissive 6 6 6
material alu0   metal Al 0
material cu15   metal Cu 0.15
material ti35   metal Ti 0.35
material au60   metal Au 0.6
material al90   metal aluminium 0.9
material ag20   metal Ag 0.2

quad -10 0 -10   20 0 0   0 0 20   floor
quad -10 0 -3    20 0 0   0 6 0    wall
quad -2 5 -1     4 0 0    0 0 3    lamp      # facing down

sphere -3.0 0.55 0  0.55  alu0
sphere -1.8 0.55 0  0.55  cu15   translate 0.6 0 0
sphere -0.6 0.55 0  0.55  ti35   translate 0.6 0 0
sphere  0.6 0.55 0  0.55  au60   translate 0.6 0 0
sphere  1.8 0.55 0  0.55  al90   translate 0.6 0 0
sphere  0.0 0.4  1.5 0.4  ag20
